        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Word of Honor, Miami Vice, Nash Bridges, The Deadliest Season, Decoration Day, Because Mommy Works, The Tuskegee Airmen, The Great Gatsby, The Pilot's Wife, Avenger\n- People: Don Johnson, Jeanne Tripplehorn, Sharon Lawrence, John Heard, Arliss Howard, Robert Markowitz, Ernest Kilroy\n- Organizations: Titus Productions, American Power Boat Association\n- Awards: Golden Globe, Hollywood Walk of Fame\n\nFacts:\n- Don Johnson was born on December 15, 1949.\n- Don Johnson is an American actor, producer, director, singer, and songwriter.\n- Don Johnson played James \"Sonny\" Crockett in the 1980s television series Miami Vice.\n- Robert Markowitz directed Decoration Day in 1990.\n- Robert Markowitz directed Because Mommy Works in 1994.\n- Robert Markowitz directed The Tuskegee Airmen in 1995.\n- Don Johnson had the lead role in the 1990s cop series Nash Bridges.\n- Robert Markowitz directed The Great Gatsby in 2000.\n- Word of Honor is an American television film released in 2003.\n- Robert Markowitz directed The Pilot's Wife in 2003.\n- Robert Markowitz directed Word of Honor in 2003.\n- Word of Honor stars Don Johnson, Jeanne Tripplehorn, Sharon Lawrence, John Heard, and Arliss Howard.\n- Robert Markowitz directed Avenger in 2006.\n- Don Johnson won a Golden Globe for Miami Vice.\n- Don Johnson was the American Power Boat Association's 1988 World Champion of the Offshore World Cup.\n- Don Johnson received a star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame.\n- The Deadliest Season was directed by Robert Markowitz.\n- The Deadliest Season was written by Ernest Kilroy.\n- The Deadliest Season was produced by Titus Productions.",
